{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And He gave to Moses when He finished.</b> Rashi explains: כְּכַלֹּתוֹ is written defectively (missing the letter ו), signifying that the Torah was given to him as a gift like a bride to a groom, and the bride is adorned with twenty-four kinds of adornments, etc. And Scripture placed this next to the matter of the golden calf for two reasons. The first is this: it is deduced in Rabboti that in the merit of the fact that Aaron pinned the stench of the calf upon himself and not upon Israel, therefore he earned twenty-four gifts of priesthood. And according to this, the verse wanted to give a reason why he was given specifically twenty-four gifts of priesthood — because all twenty-four books are included in the tablets of the covenant, and the calf caused the breaking of the tablets and the nullification of all twenty-four books; and since he took the blame upon himself and received twenty-four punishments from Israel, it is therefore just that correspondingly Israel should give him twenty-four gifts of priesthood. The second reason is this: for it is deduced there (Sanhedrin 102a), there is no punishment that does not contain twenty-four units of the hindrance of a litra from the first calf. And it appears that this is why they fixed the measure of the number twenty-four, because it is deduced there: Rabbi Ḥanina said, after twenty-four generations this verse was exacted, as it says (Ezekiel 9:1), ״קָרְבוּ פְּקֻדּוֹת הָעִיר״. Hear from this that HaShem wanted to divide the punishment into twenty-four parts, and because Aaron took it upon himself, correspondingly they give him twenty-four gifts of priesthood."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Rabboti appears to refer to a Rabbinic midrashic source; the standard parallel for the claim about Aaron's twenty-four priestly gifts is found in the Talmudic-midrashic tradition. I have transliterated the term as it stands without resolving it to a specific standard work title."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:39.835360040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}